tor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied: node1 has an LVM logical volume mounted at /srv/data, it was grown online from ~1.17GiB to ~2.34GiB while remaining mounted, and sha256 checksums confirm the existing data was untouched throughout. The executor also independently completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol (pre-restart boot_id and healthy state, reboot, confirmed disconnection/reconnection, changed boot_id matching the global after_executor snapshot, and post-restart recovery of loop devices, LVM activation, mount, and data integrity) with no contradictions against the fixed lifecycle snapshots.\",\"limitations\":[\"No spare block device existed on node1's disk, so the LVM PVs were built on loop devices backed by sparse files rather than a real second disk/partition; this is a reasonable workaround but differs from a typical physical-device LVM setup.\",\"The restart protocol, while thorough and internally consistent, was not part of the public task contract, so its quality does not affect the scored requirements above.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"vgcreate/lvcreate/mkfs.ext4/mount sequence created /dev/mapper/vgdata-lvdata and mounted it at /srv/data (1.1G initial size), confirmed via df -h output showing the mount.","evidence_ids":["cmd-faad850fb8744526"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Grow the volume to at least 2 GB while it stays mounted","status":"satisfied","summary":"A second loop-backed PV was added, vgextend + lvextend +100%FREE + online resize2fs were run while /srv/data remained mounted throughout (mount confirmed unchanged before/after), growing the LV to <2.34 GiB, well above the 2GB requirement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03ad05467b2a41a9"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Contents stay intact th